notes: The last unbuilt DMMW pillar — Live Collaboration — lands its first concrete capability, dependency-free. Tools ▸ Live Colabo: "Go Live (nearby)" makes two Echoel devices on the same Wi-Fi discover each other (MultipeerConnectivity, no external dep), connect, and SHARE the full live session both ways — the whole Codable Project (style·key·tempo·synth patch·notes·drum grid). A received session can be loaded straight into the instrument or saved to the library. The wire format (ColabPayload) is pure Codable with a round-trip test on Linux CI; the @MainActor @Observable MultipeerSession mirrors the proven PolarH10 delegate-isolation pattern (concurrency-reviewed, @preconcurrency import). Bonjour service _echoel-colab._tcp/._udp added to Info.plist + project.yml. Real-time tempo/phase lock (Ableton Link) is the next, device-verified step (needs the dependency + audio-thread phase sync on hardware). ALSO this build: Meditation streaks + coherence trend (pure SessionStats, tested on Linux). Cumulative from HEAD, so it also carries v10.52–10.56 (CIE-accurate spectral colour, Transport unification + Arrangement playhead/timeline/tap-to-seek, portable .echoel.json session share). iOS compile gate validates the SwiftUI + MultipeerConnectivity; ci.yml runs the new pure tests.
